{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:50db0e50b824881672b05c68780802e99064f9e3e3035786d5c74ba23a8cf8f1","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026#cas:main","title":"Cycle density and Casimir contraction"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/db577f8f1b3b86cd11bc75b3.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Theorem","generation_id":"sha256:fda4c3462963b650c538e2177794811eb1c221b267efea4b091fd6e397533f81","id":"r:Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026:cas:main","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026","name":"Cycle density and Casimir contraction","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":"8.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","binding":{"file":"build/sections/07-casimir.tex","label":"cas:main","line":37,"manuscript":"Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026","statement_sha256":"a46280e5cb40c41c1ddfa30711e3a85d152497dd4bfcc0b186752e00e6f2ea61"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026.html#cas:main","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":8,"section_title":"Cycle traces and contraction by the transposition Casimir","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:f2fe6aaa310cbf8472211396c9c660a1009c52fdb1e72ba4ef8fc7ebbe7ad8af","file":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/07-casimir.tex","line":37,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"a46280e5cb40c41c1ddfa30711e3a85d152497dd4bfcc0b186752e00e6f2ea61","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/07-casimir.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:f2fe6aaa310cbf8472211396c9c660a1009c52fdb1e72ba4ef8fc7ebbe7ad8af","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/07-casimir.tex#L37"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{cas:main}\nThere are absolute constants $a,C>0$ such that for every dyadic $n$,\nevery $1\\le k\\le n$, and every $x\\in X_{n,k}$,\n\\[\n \\|R_x\\|_{L^{65/64}(u_{n,k})}\\le e^{C h_n(k)}.\n\\]\nFor every nontrivial partition $\\lambda\\vdash n$, put $k=n-\\lambda_1$.\nThen\n\\[\n \\|K_n(\\lambda)\\|_{\\op}\\le e^{-a h_n(k)},\\qquad\n D_\\lambda\\Tr K_n(\\lambda)^{65}\\le e^{C h_n(k)}.\n\\]\nConsequently there is an absolute integer $l$ for which\n$\\|\\mu_n^{*l}-U_{S_n}\\|_{\\TV}\\to0$ as $n\\to\\infty$ through powers of two.\nHere $U_{S_n}$ is the uniform permutation law and total variation includes\nthe factor $1/2$.  The same bound holds from every deterministic initial\npermutation.  When $n=2^d$, these $l$ sweeps take $ld$ physical shuffles."}
